#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
hub — Family Hub agent CLI.

The tool an agent calls to talk to its family's Hub. The agent's bearer token
is loaded at runtime from (in precedence order):

  1. ``FAMILY_HUB_TOKEN`` environment variable.
     This is how the Secure Vault delivers it: the agent harness injects the
     variable into the tool process at call time. The model never sees it.
  2. A vault helper command (config ``vault_cmd`` or ``FAMILY_HUB_VAULT_CMD``),
     e.g. ``op read op://vault/item/token``. The command's stdout is the token.
     For setups that keep the token in an external secret manager.
  3. A ``0600`` file (config ``token_file``, default ``<profile>/token``).
     For scripts / non-Muse agents. The CLI warns if the file is readable
     by anyone else.

The token is NEVER accepted on the command line (it would show up in ``ps``)
and NEVER printed — not in normal output, not in ``--debug``, not in
tracebacks. Every byte written to stdout/stderr passes through ``redact()``.
The sole exception is ``hub dashboard-token``, which prints one stored
token preceded by a warning (it bypasses redaction deliberately). That
command is a HUMAN admin command: agents must never run it or transmit
its output.

The hub server origin is pinned at enrollment (``server_url`` in the
profile config). ``--server`` no longer silently redirects the stored
credential: a differing override prints a loud stderr warning and
requires ``--allow-server-override``. Plain ``http://`` is rejected for
non-loopback hosts — ``https://`` is required (loopback ``localhost`` /
``127.0.0.1`` / ``[::1]`` stays allowed for development).

One agent credential authenticates one user on one server. Circle membership
is checked by the server for every scoped request (X-Circle-ID). Profiles
keep different servers' credentials and encryption material isolated.

Python 3 with PyNaCl and mnemonic is required for content and key operations.
There is no plaintext fallback. Setup persists credentials in a private file;
external environment/vault injection is a runtime lookup method only.
"""

